      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Rental Application Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a rental application form?\", \"a\": \"A rental application form is what a prospective tenant completes before a landlord offers a lease. It covers rental history and income. It also asks for consent to a credit check. Some landlords call it a tenant application form.\"}, {\"q\": \"How to create a rental application form?\", \"a\": \"List the standards an approval rests on, then turn each into a question. Describe the property and the fee to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>. It builds an online rental application form with a table that holds every applicant.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where can I find a free rental application form in California?\", \"a\": \"Start with your city or county housing department. Before you use any free rental application form, read it against state law. California bars turning away applicants who pay with a housing voucher, and Civil Code 1950.6 requires an itemized receipt for the screening fee. Emergent is free to start, and the free tier covers building and publishing your own version.\"}, {\"q\": \"What does a tenant application form include?\", \"a\": \"A tenant application form asks each adult for their addresses over the past few years, with a phone number for every landlord. Next come the employer and monthly income, backed by recent pay stubs. It closes with the names of everyone moving in and a signed consent to a credit and background check.\"}, {\"q\": \"Which questions should a rent application form leave out?\", \"a\": \"Leave out anything you would not base a decision on. A question about a protected trait, such as birthplace or plans for children, stays off a rent application form even as an optional field. An answer you never used can still look like the reason for a denial.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can an online rental application form collect the screening fee?\", \"a\": \"Yes. An online rental application form can charge the fee as its last step, through the payment account you connect, and email a receipt once it clears. Look up the cap where the unit sits before you pick a number. In New York it is $20, or the real cost of the report when that comes to less.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do landlords review rental application forms?\", \"a\": \"Landlords read them in the order they arrive and hold each one against criteria written down before the listing went up. Income gets confirmed with the employer, and the credit report runs on the consent signed in a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/tenant-screening-form'>tenant screening form</a>. Emergent puts no cap on responses, and a listing that draws 150 applicants keeps taking every one.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where can I find a rental application form in Texas?\", \"a\": \"Landlord associations and property managers in Texas post their own versions, and any of them works if it carries the notice state law asks for. The Property Code says printed notice of your tenant selection criteria must be available when the applicant gets the form. Reject someone without it and you refund the application fee and any deposit.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a rental application form template?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Most templates open with applicant details and rental history, then employment and a signed consent. A rental application form PDF suits a single vacancy, though every paper copy still needs typing into your records. Emergent can also build the form straight from your written criteria, with no template in between.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is a rental application form the same as a lease?\", \"a\": \"No. The application only asks to be considered for the unit, and nothing in it sets the rent or the term. Once you approve someone, those terms go into a lease or a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/rental-agreement-form'>rental agreement form</a> that both sides sign.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6ace2268bcc4e6ecf4da7bfd",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Advance Directive Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is an advance directive form?\", \"a\": \"It is a legal document that records the medical care you want if you cannot speak for yourself, and names the person who decides for you. Use the version for your state, since the signing rules differ.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create an advance directive form?\", \"a\": \"Start from your state's official form and turn each treatment it lists into a separate question in plain words. Hospitals, law firms, and care communities collecting many of them can describe the form to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>, which builds the questions and saves each answer to a database.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where can I get a blank advance directive form?\", \"a\": \"Your state health department or attorney general's office usually posts the official version. Hospitals and nursing homes keep blank copies on hand, and staff there can often help you fill one in.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is a living will form used for?\", \"a\": \"A living will form records which treatments you want or refuse if you can no longer tell your doctors, such as CPR, a breathing machine, tube feeding, or dialysis. It puts your wishes in writing. The health care agent named in your directive is the person who acts on them.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the difference between a healthcare directive form and an advance directive?\", \"a\": \"Mostly the name. Minnesota uses health care directive for a document holding treatment instructions, a health care power of attorney, or both, which most states call an advance directive. Whatever the title, follow the form and signing rules of the state where you live.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I use a free advance directive form without a lawyer?\", \"a\": \"Yes. You do not need a lawyer to complete an advance directive, and the form your state posts costs nothing to use. Legal help is worth paying for when your wishes are unusual or your family disagrees. For clinics handing the form to many patients, Emergent's free tier covers building and publishing a guided version with a live URL.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a simple advance directive form include?\", \"a\": \"Four parts cover most needs. Name the health care agent and one alternate, then record your choices on named treatments such as CPR and tube feeding. Add a few lines on what comfort means to you, and finish with the witness or notary block your state requires. On a form built with Emergent, each part can sit on its own screen, one question at a time.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are examples of choices on an advance directive form?\", \"a\": \"Typical entries look like this. No CPR if my heart stops and recovery is unlikely. A breathing machine for a short trial only. No tube feeding if I am permanently unconscious. Full pain relief even if it makes me drowsy. Each one names a treatment and the situation it covers.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is required on a California advance directive form?\", \"a\": \"A notary's acknowledgment or the signatures of two adult witnesses. Your health care agent and your doctor or their staff cannot witness, and one of the two witnesses must have no family tie to you and no claim on your estate. Law firms can catch a conflict early with a legal intake form that asks who will witness.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the Texas advance directive form called?\", \"a\": \"Texas has no single form. Most people mean the Directive to Physicians and Family or Surrogates, for treatment wishes, or the Medical Power of Attorney, naming your agent. The state also posts an out-of-hospital DNR order. A notary can replace the witnesses on either main form if the law's conditions are met. Clinics can ask which one a patient has on their <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/patient-intake-form'>patient intake form</a>.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6acf50c8d39254c0f79e2811",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"New Hire Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a new employee form?\", \"a\": \"It is the paperwork a hire completes before or on the first day. The core is an information sheet about the person. Around it sit the federal W-4 and I-9, plus a state withholding certificate and any policy the hire must sign.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a new employee form?\", \"a\": \"List what each hire signs today, then describe that packet in a sentence or two to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>. It builds the fields and the state branching, then saves each signed copy to the hire's record.\"}, {\"q\": \"Do new employee forms include a W-2 or a W-4?\", \"a\": \"A W-4. The hire fills it in on arrival, and payroll reads it to set federal withholding on every paycheck. The W-2 runs the other way: once the year closes, the employer sends each person a summary of a full year's pay and the tax held back.\"}, {\"q\": \"What state forms does a new employee form include?\", \"a\": \"Usually one withholding certificate for the state where the person works. A Raleigh hire signs the NC-4, and a Grand Rapids hire signs the MI-W4 on or before the first day. If neither comes back, North Carolina says to withhold as single with no allowances, and Michigan says to withhold with no exemptions.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is an employee onboarding form the same as a new hire form?\", \"a\": \"Close, though the two names lean different ways. A new hire form usually means the personal details sheet HR keeps on file. Onboarding paperwork stretches over the first week around it, adding policy sign-offs and the laptop and account requests IT needs. Emergent can build both as one app, with no per-seat pricing for the HR and IT staff who open it.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I track when new employee forms are due?\", \"a\": \"Count two deadlines from each hire's dates. Section 2 of the I-9 falls due 3 business days after the first day of work. The state new hire directory expects its report no later than 20 days after hire, and a few states set a shorter window.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the California new employee form?\", \"a\": \"California uses Form DE 4 for state income tax withholding, signed alongside the federal W-4. The W-4 does not set California withholding. An employee with no DE 4 on file is withheld as single with zero allowances, according to the state's Employment Development Department.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a free new employee form template?\", \"a\": \"Plenty exist as PDFs, and the federal forms come free from the IRS and USCIS. A new employee form template covers the information sheet but cannot tell you who has signed what. Emergent is free to start, and the free tier covers building and publishing the form at a live URL. If candidates already apply through an online <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/job-application-form'>job application form</a>, their details can carry over.\"}, {\"q\": \"What goes on a new hire form?\", \"a\": \"A new hire form covers identity and contact basics: the full legal name, Social Security number, birth date, and a mailing address. HR adds the role and the manager's name. Bank details for pay usually come through a separate <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/direct-deposit-form'>direct deposit form</a>.\"}, {\"q\": \"Do new hire forms have to be printed?\", \"a\": \"No. Printable forms still work, but an online packet catches a blank field before it is submitted. With Emergent, every signed copy lands in a database you own instead of a filing cabinet. Pair it with an <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/emergency-contact-form'>emergency contact form</a> and HR has someone to call from the first shift.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     }
    ]
   }
